"""Bazel layer for the playtest e2e fixtures (battery tier pilot).

Scope — which fixtures are Bazel-built and which stay cargo-native:

  Bazel: the 8 single-crate fixtures (alien_cake_addict, breakout,
         contributors, desk_toy, game_menu, known_answer, loading_screen,
         mines). Each is one upstream Bevy showcase game with the
         feature-gated playtest transform applied by
         scripts/fetch_bevy_examples.sh: plain builds contain ZERO
         bevy_playtest code; `playtest`-featured builds run the battery.

  cargo: thetawave — a multi-crate fork port (3 internal path crates +
         bevy_rapier2d, bevy_kira_audio, bevy_asset_loader) whose graph
         is deliberately not worth the Bazel translation cost for this
         pilot. It keeps running under cargo in the same CI job.

Generated-source caveat: fixtures/<name>/src and the per-fixture
Cargo.toml are GENERATED by scripts/fetch_bevy_examples.sh (only
tests/ and thetawave are committed wholesale). This package and the
per-fixture packages therefore ANALYZE SUCCESSFULLY ONLY AFTER the
fetch script has run. CI order: fetch step BEFORE bazel.

Battery mechanics under Bazel (vs cargo):
  - cargo satisfies `env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_fixture_<name>")` in
    tests/playtest.rs automatically; Bazel supplies the same env!()
    constant via rustc_env + $(location) on the rust_test. No
    committed fixture file is modified.
  - assets: each fixture's assets/ dir is a data dep (runfiles) of
    BOTH binary and test; the battery's own cwd isolation
    (populate_symlink_tree in bevy_playtest's battery.rs) links cwd
    entries into the child cwd, so games find ./assets exactly as
    under cargo.
"""

# Exports so crate_universe can label-reference the workspace manifest
# and lockfile from MODULE.bazel (crate.from_cargo labels:
# "//fixtures:Cargo.toml", "//fixtures:Cargo.lock").
exports_files(
    [
        "Cargo.toml",
        "Cargo.lock",
    ],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)

# All eight Bazel-built fixtures in one target for humans and CI:
#   bazelisk test --test_arg=--test-threads=1 //fixtures:playtest_battery
# (--test-threads=1 because loading_screen's tests/playtest.rs
# env-mutates via unsafe set_var, same reason as the cargo tier).
test_suite(
    name = "playtest_battery",
    tests = [
        "//fixtures/alien_cake_addict:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/breakout:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/contributors:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/desk_toy:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/game_menu:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/known_answer:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/loading_screen:playtest_battery",
        "//fixtures/mines:playtest_battery",
    ],
)
